    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2X5GbEkTg1acJJLTffK42Xc)_\n\nFollows #204. In `sp-author-notes`, an unquoted `pub-author` piece with more than one comma (`Francisco López-Muñoz, Gabriel Rubio, Juan D. Molina, Cecilio Alam`) was read as one name. It is now its own case:\n- The report has a section \"Lists of names with commas, to disambiguate\" with the split it proposes: each piece a name when the first piece has two words or more, `Last, First` pairs (flipped) when it is one word and the count is even, no proposal otherwise.\n- When the changes are written you are asked whether to split it (`sp-author-notes-disambiguate-function`, default `y-or-n-p`). Yes makes one author and one `:person:` note per name; no leaves the text as it is.\n- One comma (`Smith, John`) is still one name; `;`, `and` and quotes work as before.\n\nTested: 15 ERT tests in Emacs 29.3 batch with a temporary vault. Not run on the real `~/notes`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAXf5syXqG5HjUbdK7)_",
